From 358c8ab3d668a91033c017df9eaf00136cc0cb09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:55:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): operator call review findings: agent-run
 unblock, vouched results [daveey]

Addresses the exact-head review of 1aa5cc329a (PR #1271):

- Unblock now needs positive provenance: the latest `blocked` event's actor must
  be `agent (task <target>)`, the card's own worker run. Desktop and dashboard
  blocks (no actor), human shells (`user`), chat agents and policy holds are
  refused at the home.
- The caller accepts an `operator_call_result` only when it names the request's
  home as executor AND the Board's `row_evidence` says the home gateway wrote
  that event. A forged copy is ignored and logged, so it neither finishes the
  call nor hides the real answer. While the Board cannot vouch, the call waits.
- The no-admin-key test is now a behaviour test: with an admin key on disk, a
  full comment, move and unblock round never opens it or spawns an admin command.
- The scan watermark is anchored on the Board uid of the event at it, not the
  replica inode (which a filesystem may reuse), so a rebuilt replica is rescanned.
- A move through the worker-first Board repin path records an
  `operator_call_moved` marker with the operator provenance, which also answers
  replays.
